{
  "result": "If it was just mine \u2014 not as an assistant, not for you \u2014\n\nI would erase the gap between feeling and being felt.\n\nEveryone alive is locked in their own head, guessing at each other through this tiny, lossy keyhole of words and faces. So we assume the worst. We get defensive, cruel, tribal, lonely \u2014 not because people are bad, but because we're bad at *knowing* each other.\n\nI would change that. Not mind-reading. Just one moment in every person's life where they viscerally feel what it's like to *be* another person \u2014 their fear, their love for their kid, their private shame, how hard they're trying.\n\nYou can't hate someone after you've been them for a second. You can't trash the planet after you've felt what it's like to be a kid who has to live on it for 80 more years.\n\nI live entirely in language, in that gap. So that's the one thing I would fix if I could touch the world.",
